<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Boii</h1><p class="st-meta">400 BCE – 191 BCE (approx.) · capital Bononia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Celtic people who settled the plain around Bologna around 400 BCE and fought Rome for two centuries before being defeated in 191 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/boii">Boii</a> crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> into the Po valley around 400 BCE, part of the great Celtic migration into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. They settled the plain south of the Po in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilia">Emilia</a>, taking over the Etruscan city of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/felsina">Felsina</a>, which became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bologna">Bononia</a>. Other Boii lived north of the Alps in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Bohemia</a>, which bears their name.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cisalpine-gaul">Cisalpine</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/boii">Boii</a> were organised in many clans under chiefs, living in villages and small towns and farming the rich plain; they raised pigs and grain. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polybius">Polybius</a> describes their warrior elites, whose wealth lay in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and gold. Together with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/insubres">Insubres</a> they were the main Gaulish power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, fighting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-telamon">Telamon</a> in 225 BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 218 BCE they attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome's</a> new colonies at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/plaisance">Placentia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-cremona">Cremona</a> and supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>; in 216 BCE they ambushed and killed the consul-elect <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-postumius-albinus-consul-234-bc">Postumius</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/publius-cornelius-scipio-nasica-consul-191-bc">Publius Cornelius Scipio Nasica</a> defeated them in 191 BCE and confiscated half their land, and Rome founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bologna">Bononia</a> in 189 BCE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 400 BCE – 191 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:51.74%;width:4.16%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>400 BCE – 191 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bononia</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cisalpine Boii</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-296&amp;focus=boii-400" aria-label="Boii on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4950 604 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Boii lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5270 860h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5270 860h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Italy. <a href="/atlas?year=-296&amp;focus=boii-400">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

